3. A change is done when `<check command>` passes. Record it in `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.
4. No secrets in the repository.
5. Keep this file a map, under 200 lines and about 4,000 estimated tokens (`<check command>` measures). Put detail where the tasks that need it meet it (an error message, a test).
6. When a check fails, fix what it reports. Never weaken, skip or delete a check, test or rule to get a pass; if a check is wrong, stop and say why.
